      "id": 1,
      "text": "Ikebukuro Station is the third-busiest station in Japan and the world.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ikebukuro",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The station’s name literally means “pond bag” (池袋), a play on words with “owl” (梟) and “bag” (袋).",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25,
        26,
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ikebukuro",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Sunshine City, a large urban theme park with an aquarium, observation deck, restaurants and hotels, sits just north of the station.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.gotokyo.org/en/destinations/northern-tokyo/ikebukuro/index.html",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The old village of Ikebukuro lay northwest of the station, and the area was once an independent municipality before becoming part of Toshima ward in 1932.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ikebukuro",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Tokyo Metropolitan Theater, opened in 1990, hosts concerts, dance and theater performances near the station.",
